{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:3413114 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:3413114 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"3413114","source":"MED","pmid":"3413114","pmcid":"PMC282029","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC282029"]},"doi":"10.1073/pnas.85.18.6622","title":"A highly conserved repetitive DNA sequence, (TTAGGG)n, present at the telomeres of human chromosomes.","authorString":"Moyzis RK, Buckingham JM, Cram LS, Dani M, Deaven LL, Jones MD, Meyne J, Ratliff RL, Wu JR.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Moyzis RK","lastName":"Moyzis","firstName":"R K","initials":"RK","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Genetics Group, LS-3, Los Alamos National Laboratory, University of California 87545."}]}},{"fullName":"Buckingham JM","lastName":"Buckingham","firstName":"J M","initials":"JM"},{"fullName":"Cram LS","lastName":"Cram","firstName":"L S","initials":"LS"},{"fullName":"Dani M","lastName":"Dani","firstName":"M","initials":"M"},{"fullName":"Deaven LL","lastName":"Deaven","firstName":"L L","initials":"LL"},{"fullName":"Jones MD","lastName":"Jones","firstName":"M D","initials":"MD"},{"fullName":"Meyne J","lastName":"Meyne","firstName":"J","initials":"J"},{"fullName":"Ratliff RL","lastName":"Ratliff","firstName":"R L","initials":"RL"},{"fullName":"Wu JR","lastName":"Wu","firstName":"J R","initials":"JR"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","related_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"18","volume":"85","journalIssueId":590418,"dateOfPublication":"1988 Sep","monthOfPublication":9,"yearOfPublication":1988,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A","title":"Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences of the United States of America","essn":"1091-6490","issn":"0027-8424","isoabbreviation":"Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A","nlmid":"7505876"},"printPublicationDate":"1988-09-01"},"pubYear":"1988","pageInfo":"6622-6626","abstractText":"A highly conserved repetitive DNA sequence, (TTAGGG)n, has been isolated from a human recombinant repetitive DNA library. Quantitative hybridization to chromosomes sorted by flow cytometry indicates that comparable amounts of this sequence are present on each human chromosome. Both fluorescent in situ hybridization and BAL-31 nuclease digestion experiments reveal major clusters of this sequence at the telomeres of all human chromosomes. The evolutionary conservation of this DNA sequence, its terminal chromosomal location in a variety of higher eukaryotes (regardless of chromosome number or chromosome length), and its similarity to functional telomeres isolated from lower eukaryotes suggest that this sequence is a functional human telomere.","affiliation":"Genetics Group, LS-3, Los Alamos National Laboratory, University of California 87545.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, U.S. Gov't, P.H.S.","Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","research-article","Research Support, U.S. Gov't, Non-P.H.S.","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"NCRR NIH HHS","acronym":"RR","grantId":"RR01315","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Chromosomes, Human","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"AN","qualifierName":"analysis"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"DNA","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"AN","qualifierName":"analysis"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Flow Cytometry"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Nucleic Acid Hybridization"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Base Sequence"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Repetitive Sequences, Nucleic Acid"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Molecular Sequence Data"}]},"chemicalList":{"chemical":[{"name":"DNA